Room: new contents opened from a Room window stay in that window's Browser.

Navigate() picks the Browser that receives a disposition in
GetBrowserAndTabForDisposition(): tabs stay in the source Browser, but
NEW_POPUP, NEW_WINDOW and NEW_PICTURE_IN_PICTURE always create a Browser of
their own (CreateBrowserWindow), and OFF_THE_RECORD finds or creates an
incognito one. For Room that Browser would get a Chrome BrowserView: a Chrome
window beside the host's (PR #1 finding 1, research/notes/
roomcore-hardening-review.md). Room's host places every new contents itself
(a Today tab under its opener, Phase 2.6), so //room answers the question
for Browsers it created: the source Browser for the popup, window and
picture-in-picture dispositions (the host reads the disposition and the
requested size from //room), a cancelled navigation for off-the-record (no
private windows before Chapter 4.8), and Chrome's own choice otherwise.

No existing hook: the only override in this path is
web_app::NavigationCapturingProcess (web apps only), the
BrowserWindow factory (patch 0003) runs after the Browser exists, and a
WebContentsDelegate wrapping Browser's would have to forward ~150 members.
The alternative without a patch, a throwaway headless Browser per popup
whose contents //room moves out afterwards, creates and tears down a full
Browser (features, session entries) for every window.open.

Phase 3.2a, 2026-10-05. //room: room/browser/room_browser_window.mm
(BrowserForDisposition).
